                <pb facs="0748" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00 Statement July 18, 1937/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-30T19:00:00-04:00">July 30, 1937—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. Your 35, July 29, 6 p.m. The final sentence of my statement of July 16 is
                    purely descriptive of the method which this Government has found suited to its
                    purposes in cooperating with other governments with a view to giving effect to
                    the principles which we advocate and which I enumerated in detail in that
                    statement. It was intended to express this Government’s willingness to cooperate
                    in any and all efforts of a peaceful and practicable nature to support the
                    principles advocated by it and set forth in my statement.</p>
                <p>You may communicate the foregoing orally to the Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
